From 6ee3434d547f6401fcf8f2b744cb5d4280f522b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 08:14:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 087/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: firmware idle with queued
 input is a stall

codec_hevc_stall_work() treats HEVC_ACTION_DONE and 0 as benign on the
grounds that the firmware is idle in NAL search waiting for data, and
starvation is not a stall. That is right only while there is nothing for
it to find.

codec_hevc_skip_slice() writes ACTION_DONE, kicks the firmware and arms
the watchdog, and it runs for every slice skipped while resynchronising to
an IRAP. If the firmware stops answering that kick the driver waits for an
interrupt that never comes, the watchdog sees ACTION_DONE, calls it benign
and re-arms - forever. Playback stops dead with no message in the log;
userspace only sees EAGAIN from every dequeue:

  CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::Reset - receive frame failed: Resource temporarily unavailable (-11)

Measured on a stream carrying one malformed frame (cu_qp_delta -34), by
reading the status register and the vdec interrupt count while it happened:

  t+0s  STATUS=0x05  LCU=0x4000027C  irq33=4191   decoding
  t+3s  STATUS=0xFF  LCU=0x40000000  irq33=5150   stopped
  t+6s  STATUS=0xFF  LCU=0x40000000  irq33=5150   frozen
  t+9s  STATUS=0xFF  LCU=0x40000000  irq33=5150   frozen

Status pinned at ACTION_DONE, interrupt count not advancing, and input
still queued. The stall detector never fired.

Distinguish the two cases with esparser_queued_bufs: idle with nothing
queued is starvation and still benign; idle with buffers queued means the
firmware has work and is not doing it. The latter falls through to the
existing progress protocol, which requires the status and LCU to hold
still across consecutive samples before recovering - so a firmware that is
merely slow to start is not disturbed.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 35 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index 1d93e451cce0..9ee8856e4061 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -1592,19 +1592,42 @@ static void codec_hevc_stall_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	status = amvdec_read_dos(core, HEVC_DEC_STATUS_REG);
 
 	/*
-	 * Benign states: 0x8/0xa = the driver owes the next action;
-	 * ACTION_DONE/0 = firmware idle in NAL search, waiting for
-	 * more stream data (starvation is not a stall).
+	 * 0x8/0xa mean the driver owes the next action, and it is about to
+	 * take it from the threaded ISR - never a stall.
 	 */
 	if (status == HEVC_SLICE_SEGMENT_DONE ||
-	    status == HEVC_DECPIC_DATA_DONE ||
-	    status == HEVC_ACTION_DONE ||
-	    status == 0) {
+	    status == HEVC_DECPIC_DATA_DONE) {
 		mod_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &hevc->stall_work,
 				 msecs_to_jiffies(STALL_TIMEOUT_MS));
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * ACTION_DONE/0 means the firmware is idle in NAL search. That is
+	 * starvation - and not a stall - only while there is nothing queued
+	 * for it to find. With source buffers sitting in the ESPARSER it has
+	 * work and is not doing it, which is a wedge.
+	 *
+	 * This matters because codec_hevc_skip_slice() parks the status at
+	 * ACTION_DONE and kicks the firmware, and that is the path taken for
+	 * every slice skipped while resynchronising to an IRAP. If the
+	 * firmware stops answering the kick, the driver waits for an
+	 * interrupt that never arrives while the watchdog re-arms forever,
+	 * and playback stops with no diagnostic at all - userspace just sees
+	 * EAGAIN from every dequeue.
+	 *
+	 * Observed on a stream carrying one malformed frame: status pinned
+	 * at 0xFF and the vdec interrupt count frozen for as long as it was
+	 * watched, with input still queued.
+	 */
+	if (status == HEVC_ACTION_DONE || status == 0) {
+		if (!atomic_read(&sess->esparser_queued_bufs)) {
+			mod_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &hevc->stall_work,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(STALL_TIMEOUT_MS));
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Everything else is one of the firmware's in-flight states - NAL
 	 * header parse (VPS/SPS/PPS/SEI/slice segment), slice decode, NAL
-- 
2.43.0

